@startuml python-provider-lifecycle
' Python provider construction, negotiation, callback, and teardown.
' Colors: Python application = blue; shared Python ABI facade = green;
' native consumer = purple; bounded lifecycle/token synchronization = amber.
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName "DejaVu Sans"
skinparam sequence {
  ArrowColor #37474F
  ArrowThickness 2
  LifeLineBorderColor #455A64
  LifeLineBackgroundColor #FAFAFA
  ParticipantBorderThickness 2
}
skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #FFF8E1
  BorderColor #F57F17
  FontColor #263238
}

title Python-hosted provider — retained ABI resource lifecycle

actor "Python application" as App #BBDEFB
participant "Provider facade\n(resource owner)" as Facade #C8E6C9
database "Lifecycle registry /\nper-context token arena" as State #FFE0B2
participant "Native Vinary Tree\nconsumer" as Native #D1C4E9
participant "Python provider object" as Provider #BBDEFB

App -> Facade: construct provider + validated options
Facade -> State: register monotonic context key\n(initial retain = 1)
Facade --> App: two-word VtResource borrow

App -> Native: call constructor with &VtResource
Native -> Facade: retain(context)
Facade -> State: increment retain under short lifecycle lock
Native -> Facade: query_interface(16-byte ID, version)
Facade --> Native: provider-owned immutable vtable

group synchronous algebra or graph callback
  Native -> Facade: invoke callback(context, borrowed inputs, out)
  Facade -> State: lock-free live-context lookup
  Facade -> State: validate/copy input leases\n(per-context lock when tokens are involved)
  Facade -> Provider: call user method with no registry/token lock held
  Provider --> Facade: immutable result or exception
  alt valid result
    Facade -> State: publish owned output lease\n(per-context lock, bounded batch)
    Facade --> Native: OK + initialized output
  else exception or malformed result
    Facade --> Native: typed status; output remains untouched
  end
end

Native -> Facade: release_values(owned leases)
Facade -> State: validate entire batch, then release atomically
Native -> Facade: release(context)
Facade -> State: decrement native retain
App -> Facade: close() / with-scope exit
Facade -> State: remove context on final retain
note over App,Native
  GC finalization is leak containment only.
  Deterministic close defines the normal lifecycle.
end note
@enduml
